# ---------------- Stonehenge ----------------
meta={
"type":"place","title_zh":"巨石阵：石头、尸骨与转折的年","title_en":"Stonehenge: Stones, Bones, and the Turning Year",
"era":"约公元前 3000–前 1500 年","era_en":"c. 3000–1500 BCE",
"region":"英国，威尔特郡，埃姆斯伯里","region_en":"Amesbury, Wiltshire, England",
"coords":[51.1789,-1.8262],"tags":["巨石阵","新石器时代","巨石建筑","英国","考古"],"collections":[],"credibility":"verified",
"related":["carnac-stones","troy"],
"en_headings":["The stone setting","Three building phases","Where the stones came from","Bones, cremation, and solstice","Who built it, and why","Management and argument today"],
"limits_zh":"巨石阵最难的三个问题仍没有一致答案：蓝石究竟怎样从威尔士运来，整个建筑序列的每一阶段由谁主持，以及它在使用中的核心功能是什么。考古地层能给出先后关系，却给不出动机；文字材料不存在，后世传说又不能当作当时人的自述。因此本文把“石头被立起来”与“为什么立起来”分开，前者可以描述，后者只能并列假说。",
"limits_en":"Three questions about Stonehenge still lack agreed answers: how the bluestones were moved from Wales, who directed each stage of the building sequence, and what the monument's central function was while it was in use. Stratigraphy can establish order but not motive; there are no written records, and later legends cannot be treated as testimony from the builders. This entry therefore separates 'the stones were raised' from 'why they were raised': the first can be described, the second can only be set out as competing hypotheses.",
}
sections=[
("一、石头的现场","巨石阵在英格兰威尔特郡的索尔兹伯里平原上，坐标大约是北纬 51 度 10 分、西经 1 度 49 分。它不是一个孤立的石圈，而是一整片被土沟、土堤、坑洞、道路和墓葬包围的遗址。今天游客看到的环形石列、三石塔和外围的沟渠，是不同时代叠加后的结果；在三千多年的使用期里，这里被反复改建、增补和废弃。1986 年，它与周边景观一起列入世界遗产；2013 年，新的游客中心在遗址以西开馆。把巨石阵当成一件一次性完成的“作品”，是理解它的第一道障碍。","The site stands on Salisbury Plain in Wiltshire, England, at roughly 51°10'N, 1°49'W. It is not an isolated stone circle but a whole landscape of ditches, banks, pits, avenues, and burials. The ring of sarsens, the trilithons, and the surrounding earthwork that visitors see today are the result of different phases layered on top of one another; over more than three thousand years the place was repeatedly rebuilt, extended, and abandoned. In 1986 it was inscribed as a World Heritage Site together with its surrounding landscape, and in 2013 a new visitor centre opened west of the stones. Treating Stonehenge as a single finished 'work' is the first obstacle to understanding it."),
("二、三个建造阶段","最早的工程大约在公元前 3000 年：一圈土沟和土堤，内侧有几十个被称为“奥布里洞”的坑，坑里后来埋入火葬遗骸。约公元前 2600 至前 2400 年，巨大的砂岩被立成外圈，并出现五组三石塔。约公元前 2400 至前 2200 年，较小的蓝石被运来并多次重排，形成今天看到的内圈结构。此后仍有墓葬和修缮，但主体工程已经结束。三个阶段之间隔了几百年，主持者、参与者和仪式内容都可能发生变化。","The earliest works date to about 3000 BCE: a circular ditch and bank, with dozens of pits known as the Aubrey Holes, some of which later received cremated human remains. Around 2600–2400 BCE, huge sarsen stones were set up in an outer circle and five trilithons were raised. Around 2400–2200 BCE, smaller bluestones were brought in and rearranged several times, producing the inner setting seen today. Later burials and repairs continued, but the main construction was over. The phases are separated by centuries, and the people, participants, and ritual content may have changed between them."),
("三、石头从哪里来","最大的砂岩块来自约 25 公里外的马尔伯勒丘陵，每块重达二十多吨；蓝石则来自约 250 公里外的威尔士普雷塞利山区。蓝石的运输方式争论了很久：一种意见认为是人类用木橇、滚木和绳索拖运，另一种意见认为是冰川在更早的冰期把它们带到平原。两种说法都能解释部分石块，却不能解释全部组合。石头的来源可以通过岩性比对确认，运输路线却仍要靠间接证据推断。","The largest sarsens came from the Marlborough Downs about 25 kilometres away, each weighing more than twenty tonnes; the bluestones came from the Preseli Hills in Wales, roughly 250 kilometres distant. How the bluestones travelled has been argued for a long time: one view has people dragging them on sledges, rollers, and ropes, another has glaciers carrying them to the plain in an earlier ice age. Each account explains some stones but not the whole assemblage. The source of the rock can be confirmed by petrological comparison; the route still has to be inferred from indirect evidence."),
("四、尸骨、火葬与至点","巨石阵的坑洞里埋着大量火葬遗骨，估计涉及一百多人，时间跨度很长。遗址的主轴指向夏至日出与冬至日落的方向，这一点在测量上很清楚；但“它是一个精确的日历”或“它能预测日月食”的说法，超出了石料本身能提供的证据。冬至的日落穿过三石塔之间的视线，是每年仍可观察的现象；夏至早晨，人群则聚在石圈中央等待日出。仪式与天象有关，但相关不等于唯一功能。","The pits at Stonehenge contain many cremated remains, perhaps involving more than a hundred people over a long period. The monument's main axis aligns with the midsummer sunrise and the midwinter sunset, and that much is clear from survey; but claims that it was a precise calendar or could predict eclipses go beyond what the stones themselves can support. The midwinter sunset through the trilithon gap is still observable each year, while crowds gather inside the circle at midsummer dawn. Ritual and sky are connected, but connection is not the same as sole function."),
("五、谁建、为什么建","参与建造的人数不会少：运输、雕刻、竖立和反复重排都需要成百上千的劳动日。考古学家在附近发现了杜灵顿墙等同期聚落，说明这里不是荒野中的孤立神庙，而是有人居住、饲养牲畜、举行宴饮的区域中心。关于目的，常见假说包括祖先崇拜、治疗、领地联合的象征、季节循环的舞台。它们彼此并不完全排斥，但也没有一个能单独解释全部阶段。把巨石阵说成“德鲁伊的神庙”或“梅林的魔法”，属于后来附会，不是考古结论。","Building on this scale took many hands: transport, shaping, raising, and repeated rearrangement all required hundreds or thousands of labour days. Archaeologists have found contemporary settlements such as Durrington Walls nearby, which shows that this was not an isolated temple in empty country but a regional centre where people lived, kept cattle, and held feasts. Proposed purposes include ancestor cult, healing, a symbol of territorial union, and a stage for the seasonal cycle. They are not mutually exclusive, but no single one explains every phase. Calling Stonehenge a 'Druid temple' or 'Merlin's magic' belongs to later invention, not archaeological conclusion."),
("六、今天的管理与争论","巨石阵周围的公路一直是个难题。A303 公路紧贴遗址，车流和噪声影响景观；修隧道的方案讨论了多年，支持者看重交通与景观，反对者担心施工破坏地下遗存。每年冬至和夏至，公众仍被允许在特定时段进入石圈，但日常参观只能沿外围步道行走。遗址的保护、游客体验和道路需求，至今仍在拉扯。","The roads around Stonehenge have long been a problem. The A303 runs close to the monument, and traffic and noise affect the landscape; a tunnel scheme has been discussed for years, with supporters stressing transport and landscape and opponents fearing damage to buried remains. The public is still allowed into the stone circle at specific times around midwinter and midsummer, but ordinary visits follow an outer path. Conservation, visitor access, and road demand remain in tension."),
]
