# ---------------- Giza ----------------
meta={
"type":"place","title_zh":"吉萨高原：三座金字塔与一座狮身人面像","title_en":"The Giza Plateau: Three Pyramids and a Sphinx",
"era":"约公元前 2580–前 2500 年","era_en":"c. 2580–2500 BCE",
"region":"埃及，吉萨，开罗西南","region_en":"Giza, southwest of Cairo, Egypt",
"coords":[29.9792,31.1342],"tags":["吉萨","金字塔","埃及","第四王朝","考古"],"collections":[],"credibility":"verified",
"related":["troy","atlantis"],
"en_headings":["Three pyramids on a plateau","Stone, casing, and construction","Workers, rations, and cemeteries","The Sphinx","From wonder to occultism","Conservation and tourism"],
"limits_zh":"吉萨的建造组织仍有大量空白：石料的具体采运路线、不同金字塔的施工顺序、工匠队伍的季节性轮换，以及狮身人面像的原始形制与年代，都缺少完整证据。所谓“隐藏通道”“地下宫殿”的探测结果，需要区分已发表的物探异常与已经打开的实地结构。本文只把有发掘、测绘或档案支撑的内容写成事实，把模型和猜测留在解释层。",
"limits_en":"Much about Giza's construction organisation remains blank: the exact quarry and transport routes, the building sequence of the individual pyramids, the seasonal rotation of work gangs, and the original form and date of the Sphinx all lack complete evidence. Claims about 'hidden passages' or 'underground palaces' must distinguish published geophysical anomalies from structures that have actually been opened. This entry treats as fact only what excavation, survey, or archival record supports, and leaves models and guesses in the interpretation layer.",
}
sections=[
("一、高原上的三座塔","吉萨高原在开罗西南，尼罗河西岸。这里最醒目的三座金字塔通常按主人称呼：胡夫的大金字塔、哈夫拉的金字塔和门卡乌拉的金字塔，旁边还有更小的王后金字塔、庙宇、堤道、墓葬和狮身人面像。它们属于埃及第四王朝，约公元前 2580 至前 2500 年。把“吉萨”等同于“胡夫金字塔”会漏掉整个建筑群：三座塔的规模、内部结构和保存状态并不相同，周围的庙宇与墓地才是理解其运作的关键。","The Giza Plateau lies southwest of Cairo, on the west bank of the Nile. Its three most conspicuous pyramids are usually named for their owners: Khufu's Great Pyramid, Khafre's pyramid, and Menkaure's pyramid, with smaller queen's pyramids, temples, causeways, tombs, and the Sphinx around them. They belong to Egypt's Fourth Dynasty, roughly 2580–2500 BCE. To equate 'Giza' with 'the Great Pyramid' is to miss the complex: the three pyramids differ in scale, internal structure, and preservation, and the surrounding temples and cemeteries are essential to understanding how the site worked."),
("二、石料、 casing 与施工","大金字塔原高约 146 米，现存约 138 米，外层的白色石灰岩 casing 大部分已被后世取走，只有哈夫拉塔顶还保留一段。核心石料主要采自高原南侧的采石场，花岗岩则从阿斯旺沿尼罗河运来。关于如何把石块提升到高处，学界提出过直线坡道、螺旋坡道、杠杆与内部通道等多种模型；没有一种模型能同时解释所有施工痕迹。可以确认的是，工程需要严密的采石、运输、供粮与人员组织，而不是“奴隶被鞭子赶上工地”的单一画面。","The Great Pyramid was originally about 146 metres high and stands about 138 metres today; most of its white limestone casing was removed in later centuries, though a patch remains at the top of Khafre's pyramid. The core stone came mainly from quarries south of the plateau, while granite was brought from Aswan along the Nile. For raising blocks, scholars have proposed straight ramps, spiral ramps, levers, and internal passages; no single model explains every construction trace. What can be confirmed is that the work required tight organisation of quarrying, transport, food supply, and labour—not the single image of slaves driven by whips."),
("三、工匠、口粮与墓地","金字塔附近的工匠聚落、面包房、啤酒作坊和墓地，改变了“谁建造了金字塔”的讨论。发掘显示，工人有组织地居住、进食和埋葬，一些人还留下了队名和涂鸦。他们不是现代意义上的自由雇佣者，但也不等于没有报酬的奴隶。劳动力可能按季节轮换，农闲时来自尼罗河沿岸的村庄。把建造者简单分成“奴隶”或“自由人”，会遮住更重要的中间状态：国家征调、口粮配给、技术分工与身份差异。","The workers' settlements, bakeries, breweries, and cemeteries near the pyramids have changed the discussion of 'who built the pyramids'. Excavation shows that workers lived, ate, and were buried in an organised way, and some left gang names and graffiti. They were not free wage labourers in the modern sense, but they were also not simply unpaid slaves. The workforce may have rotated seasonally, coming from villages along the Nile in the agricultural off-season. Reducing the builders to 'slaves' or 'free men' hides the more important intermediate status: state conscription, food rations, technical division of labour, and differences of rank."),
("四、狮身人面像","狮身人面像长约 73 米、高约 20 米，由整块石灰岩凿成，面朝东方。它的年代、原始面貌和建造者仍有争论：主流观点把它放在哈夫拉时期，但也有人根据侵蚀形态提出更早的年代。所谓“梦碑”记录了一位法老清理沙土后得到梦谕的故事，属于后期文本，不能直接当作建造记录。侵蚀是另一条证据线：盐、风、地下水和历史上的清理都在改变石面，单靠侵蚀形态断代并不可靠。","The Sphinx is about 73 metres long and 20 metres high, carved from a single outcrop of limestone and facing east. Its date, original appearance, and builder are still debated: the mainstream places it in Khafre's reign, while others argue for an earlier date from erosion patterns. The 'Dream Stele' records a later king's dream after clearing sand, but it is a later text and cannot be read directly as a construction record. Erosion is another evidence line: salt, wind, groundwater, and historical clearance have all changed the surface, so dating from erosion alone is unreliable."),
("五、从“奇迹”到“神秘学”","19 世纪以来，吉萨被反复写进神秘学、民族主义叙事和通俗文化。常见的说法包括“金字塔是精确的历法计算机”“比例里藏着圆周率”“它是外星人或失落文明的产物”。这些说法往往把可测量的几何关系与有意的设计混为一谈：金字塔确实有精确的朝向和尺度，但“精确”不等于“超自然”。埃及学家的工作不是否认神秘感，而是把可验证的测量、当时的文献和后世的添加分开。","Since the nineteenth century, Giza has been repeatedly written into occultism, nationalist narratives, and popular culture. Common claims include 'the pyramid is a precise calendrical computer', 'its proportions encode pi', or 'it is the product of aliens or a lost civilisation'. Such claims often confuse measurable geometry with intentional design: the pyramids do have precise orientation and dimensions, but precision is not the same as the supernatural. The work of Egyptology is not to deny wonder but to separate verifiable survey, contemporary documents, and later additions."),
("六、保护与旅游","吉萨高原在 1979 年作为“孟菲斯及其墓地”的一部分列入世界遗产。今天它面对的是地下水上升、盐蚀、城市扩张、盗掘和大量游客。大埃及博物馆在开罗附近开放后，部分文物与参观压力得到分流，但高原本身的承载能力仍有限。保护方案常要在“开放”与“封闭”之间选择：完全封闭能减缓风化，却会让遗址脱离公众；完全开放能带来收入，却加速损耗。","Giza was inscribed in 1979 as part of 'Memphis and its Necropolis'. Today it faces rising groundwater, salt erosion, urban expansion, looting, and heavy visitation. The opening of the Grand Egyptian Museum near Cairo has diverted some objects and visitor pressure, but the plateau itself still has limited carrying capacity. Conservation plans often choose between openness and closure: total closure slows weathering but separates the site from the public; total openness brings revenue but accelerates wear."),
]
