# ---------------- Machu Picchu ----------------
meta={
"type":"place","title_zh":"马丘比丘：云端上的印加庄园","title_en":"Machu Picchu: An Inca Estate Above the Clouds",
"era":"约 1450–1572 年","era_en":"c. 1450–1572 CE",
"region":"秘鲁，库斯科大区，乌鲁班巴省","region_en":"Urubamba Province, Cusco Region, Peru",
"coords":[-13.1631,-72.5450],"tags":["马丘比丘","印加","安第斯","秘鲁","考古"],"collections":[],"credibility":"verified",
"related":["sacsayhuaman","sipan"],
"en_headings":["A city on a ridge","Inca masonry and water","Bingham and the 'discovery' story","Construction, use, and abandonment","Restoration, tourism, and carrying capacity","Return of objects and research"],
"limits_zh":"马丘比丘的建造者、用途和废弃过程仍有争议。它是不是帕查库提的皇家庄园、是否兼具宗教与行政功能、在西班牙征服后何时彻底空置，都没有单一答案。游客看到的石墙经过修复，部分区域的重建改变了原貌；早期探险者的叙述又带有“发现空白”的偏见。本文把测绘、发掘与修复记录放在前面，把“失落之城”的浪漫叙事放在后面。",
"limits_en":"The builders, function, and abandonment of Machu Picchu remain disputed. Whether it was a royal estate of Pachacuti, whether it combined religious and administrative functions, and when it was finally emptied after the Spanish conquest all lack a single answer. The walls visitors see have been restored, and reconstruction in some areas changed the original appearance; early explorers' accounts also carried a 'discovery of emptiness' bias. This entry puts survey, excavation, and restoration records first and the romantic 'lost city' narrative second.",
}
sections=[
("一、山脊上的城","马丘比丘在秘鲁库斯科大区的乌鲁班巴省，海拔约 2430 米，坐落在乌鲁班巴河上方的一道山脊上。遗址由石墙、梯田、广场、庙宇、住宅和水利系统组成，背后是华纳比丘峰。它不是一座被云雾完全遮住的“空中城市”，而是一处经过精确选址的皇家庄园：背靠山峰，面向河谷，水源、排水和滑坡风险都被纳入设计。","Machu Picchu lies in Urubamba Province, Cusco Region, Peru, at about 2,430 metres, on a ridge above the Urubamba River. The site consists of stone walls, terraces, plazas, temples, residences, and a water system, with Huayna Picchu behind it. It is not an 'air city' wholly hidden by cloud but a carefully sited royal estate: backed by the mountain, facing the valley, with water, drainage, and landslide risk built into the design."),
("二、印加的石工与水利","马丘比丘的墙体多用“干砌”技术：石块经过切割，彼此咬合，不用砂浆也能稳定。重要的建筑和庙宇使用更精细的多边形石，普通住宅则相对粗糙。遗址有引水渠、泉眼、蓄水池和排水口，雨季的水被引导到梯田和排水沟，避免冲刷地基。梯田不只是景观，它们固定土壤、提供耕作面，也承担排水功能。","Much of Machu Picchu's masonry uses dry-stone technique: blocks are cut and fitted to interlock without mortar. Important buildings and temples use finer polygonal stone, while ordinary houses are rougher. The site has channels, springs, reservoirs, and drains; rainwater is directed to terraces and drainage channels to prevent erosion of foundations. The terraces are not merely scenery: they stabilise soil, provide cultivation surfaces, and help drain water."),
("三、宾厄姆与“发现”叙事","1911 年，美国探险家海勒姆·宾厄姆在寻找印加最后的抵抗据点时，被当地向导带到马丘比丘。他后来写书，把这里描述成一座被遗忘的城市。但当地农民一直知道遗址的存在，也有家庭在附近耕作；宾厄姆的“发现”是外部视角的叙事。更重要的是，他带走并拍摄了大量器物，后来引发了秘鲁与耶鲁大学之间长达数十年的归还争议。","In 1911 the American explorer Hiram Bingham, searching for the last Inca stronghold, was led to Machu Picchu by local guides. He later wrote that it was a forgotten city. But local farmers had always known the site and some families cultivated nearby; Bingham's 'discovery' is an outside narrative. More importantly, he took and photographed many objects, which later led to a decades-long dispute between Peru and Yale University over their return."),
("四、建造、使用与废弃","考古研究把马丘比丘的主要建造期放在 15 世纪中叶，约在帕查库提统治时期。它可能是皇家庄园、宗教中心、行政节点和农业实验场的组合，而不是单一功能的城市。西班牙征服后，印加国家瓦解，马丘比丘逐渐失去维护；但它何时完全空置、是否仍有少量人口居住，仍缺少连续证据。把“废弃”说成一夜之间发生，是后世叙事常见的简化。","Archaeological research places the main construction of Machu Picchu in the mid-fifteenth century, roughly during Pachacuti's reign. It may have combined a royal estate, religious centre, administrative node, and agricultural laboratory rather than serving a single function. After the Spanish conquest the Inca state collapsed and Machu Picchu lost its maintenance; but when it was completely emptied, and whether a small population remained, still lacks continuous evidence. Describing the abandonment as a single overnight event is a common simplification of later accounts."),
("五、修复、旅游与承载量","马丘比丘在 1983 年列入世界遗产。20 世纪的清理和修复让大量建筑重新露出，但也改变了部分墙体和梯田的原貌。今天它面对的是游客压力、山体滑坡、洪水、火車与道路带来的侵蚀，以及遗址周边的城市扩张。秘鲁当局实行分时预约、单行路线和每日上限，试图在收入与保护之间取得平衡。","Machu Picchu was inscribed as a World Heritage Site in 1983. Twentieth-century clearance and restoration exposed much of the architecture but also changed the appearance of some walls and terraces. Today it faces visitor pressure, landslides, floods, erosion from trains and roads, and urban expansion around the site. Peruvian authorities use timed entry, one-way routes, and daily caps to balance revenue and conservation."),
("六、文物归还与研究","2011 年前后，耶鲁大学向秘鲁归还了数千件宾厄姆当年带走的器物，并在库斯科设立研究机构。归还解决了部分所有权争议，却没有结束研究争论：器物的年代、用途和出土位置需要重新核对，早期记录中的误差也要纠正。马丘比丘不是一座已经“写完”的遗址，它的档案仍在被重读。","Around 2011 Yale University returned thousands of objects Bingham had taken to Peru and helped establish a research institution in Cusco. The return resolved part of the ownership dispute but did not end research debate: the objects' dates, functions, and find spots need rechecking, and errors in early records need correction. Machu Picchu is not a site whose file is 'finished'; its archive is still being reread."),
]
